The test suite included with Python’s library, [Lib/test/test\_generators.py](https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.9/Lib/test/test_generators.py), contains a number of more interesting examples. Here’s one generator that implements an in-order traversal of a tree using generators recursively.

```python
# A recursive generator that generates Tree leaves in in-order.
def inorder(t):
    if t:
        for x in inorder(t.left):
            yield x

        yield t.label

        for x in inorder(t.right):
            yield x
```

Two other examples in test\_generators.py produce solutions for the N-Queens problem (placing N queens on an NxN chess board so that no queen threatens another) and the Knight’s Tour (finding a route that takes a knight to every square of an NxN chessboard without visiting any square twice).

