Either of these can be used in place of a format string, to allow {}- or \$-formatting to be used to build the actual “message” part which appears in the formatted log output in place of “%(message)s” or “{message}” or “\$message”. It’s a little unwieldy to use the class names whenever you want to log something, but it’s quite palatable if you use an alias such as \_\_ (double underscore — not to be confused with \_, the single underscore used as a synonym/alias for gettext. gettext() or its brethren).

