## Trailing “non-participatory” elements stripped

A set of parentheses that doesn't participate in the final match yields an empty string$^{\dagger}$ in the corresponding \$matches element. One caveat is that elements for trailing non-participating captures are not even included in \$matches. In the previous example, if the [(\d+) participated in the match, \$matches[3] gets a number. If it didn't participate, \$matches[3] doesn't even exist in the array.

